WEBVTT

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:54.618
This isn't the classroom.

00:00:54.702 --> 00:00:58.622
It's right around the corner.
Go on. Let's go. Come.

00:01:14.346 --> 00:01:15.222
Isn't that Ms. Seo?

00:01:30.112 --> 00:01:31.071
Let me help you.

00:01:33.699 --> 00:01:35.117
Don't you steal mine…

00:01:41.874 --> 00:01:43.000
Ji-yeon. What's wrong?

00:01:55.596 --> 00:01:56.555
Let me carry them.

00:01:56.639 --> 00:01:59.642
But I need to go to class.
I have the mock exam tomorrow.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.062
I'll take you to your class.

00:02:03.687 --> 00:02:04.647
Do you know where it is?

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:05.940
Yes, I do.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.111
Honey!
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:02:12.404 --> 00:02:15.366
What's wrong?
What is wrong with her? Honey?

00:02:15.449 --> 00:02:18.035
Hospital first, Min-woo.
Let's take her to the hospital.

00:02:20.162 --> 00:02:22.539
I'll call you. Let me take her.

00:02:24.041 --> 00:02:24.959
Let's go.

00:02:29.088 --> 00:02:30.130
Wait.

00:02:46.438 --> 00:02:47.439
Let's go.

00:03:37.781 --> 00:03:38.615
Are you okay?

00:03:40.492 --> 00:03:41.618
Where are we going?

00:03:41.702 --> 00:03:44.079
I called Dr. Kim. We will--

00:03:44.163 --> 00:03:45.205
Go home.

00:03:45.998 --> 00:03:48.584
Hospital first. Let's do that, will you?

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.587
I just want to go home and rest. Later.

00:04:01.263 --> 00:04:06.018
Ms. Seo's doctor said so,
and I did some research too.

00:04:06.101 --> 00:04:08.562
If she stops taking it, she'll be okay.

00:04:10.606 --> 00:04:13.984
It might take some time,
but she'll recover.

00:04:14.777 --> 00:04:15.944
How can a person…

00:04:17.821 --> 00:04:20.032
do such a thing?

00:04:23.452 --> 00:04:25.788
He is her husband and her family.

00:04:26.914 --> 00:04:28.624
We have to pretend we don't know.

00:04:29.625 --> 00:04:31.960
Ms. Seo is very careful about it too.

00:04:32.044 --> 00:04:34.630
I'm also looking into this.
We need more time.

00:04:35.839 --> 00:04:37.091
What should I do?

00:04:37.174 --> 00:04:40.219
Run the company soundly?

00:04:53.941 --> 00:04:55.067
I want to rest.

00:04:58.362 --> 00:05:00.697
Will you be okay by yourself?
Do you want to go home?

00:05:02.658 --> 00:05:04.243
I'll call you later.

00:05:08.956 --> 00:05:09.957
Okay.

00:05:18.173 --> 00:05:19.508
Back then…

00:05:21.927 --> 00:05:25.097
when you came to see me at the airport,

00:05:26.932 --> 00:05:28.225
did you know about this?

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.441
Yes.

00:05:41.488 --> 00:05:42.489
Okay.

00:06:28.785 --> 00:06:31.163
IN-COMPANY BULLETIN BOARD
WHAT'S GOING ON IN JARIM?

00:06:31.246 --> 00:06:33.707
IS IT TRUE THAT JARIM CEO HAS DEMENTIA?
MY SHARES…

00:06:45.761 --> 00:06:48.138
This isn't right.
Let's go to the hospital.

00:06:48.222 --> 00:06:50.933
I should've told you in advance.

00:06:52.059 --> 00:06:54.561
Sometimes, these symptoms appear.

00:06:54.645 --> 00:06:57.397
Then why didn't you tell me?

00:06:57.481 --> 00:06:59.858
You should've gone to the hospital first.

00:06:59.942 --> 00:07:02.236
Why did you suffer alone? This upsets me.

00:07:02.778 --> 00:07:04.363
I did go to the hospital.

00:07:08.992 --> 00:07:11.745
What did the doctor say?
Why is it happening to you?

00:07:13.288 --> 00:07:15.207
It's the side effect of a drug.

00:07:15.874 --> 00:07:18.835
The medicine I stopped taking
is the issue.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:29.972
Was Ji-woo there too?
Her shoes were on me…

00:07:30.681 --> 00:07:33.433
Oh, right. I need to call Ji-woo.

00:07:34.142 --> 00:07:36.436
-Everyone was shocked.
-I'll do it.

00:07:38.605 --> 00:07:40.649
JI-WOO

00:07:42.276 --> 00:07:44.987
Anyway, what was that reporter
doing in the company?

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:47.239
I called him.

00:07:48.073 --> 00:07:49.116
Why did you?

00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:52.452
I had to find some info.
Honey, let me make this call first.

00:08:03.505 --> 00:08:05.382
I was almost in trouble, wasn't I?

00:08:06.508 --> 00:08:07.426
Yes.

00:08:07.509 --> 00:08:12.347
If it hadn't been for Kyeong-do,
I would've kept taking that drug.

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:15.100
I avoided the crisis thanks to him.

00:08:16.768 --> 00:08:17.769
Yes.

00:08:21.648 --> 00:08:22.649
Are you mad?

00:08:23.233 --> 00:08:24.234
Yes.

00:08:28.322 --> 00:08:29.156
No.

00:08:38.582 --> 00:08:40.751
You must have been scared by yourself.

00:08:45.756 --> 00:08:50.010
I had no idea
and insisted on going to England.

00:08:50.635 --> 00:08:52.846
I tried to run away alone and save myself.

00:08:54.431 --> 00:08:56.641
You must've been so frustrated back then.

00:08:56.725 --> 00:09:00.645
Yes. I was so frustrated
that I threatened Kyeong-do.

00:09:03.565 --> 00:09:04.399
Ji-yeon.

00:09:05.817 --> 00:09:09.446
I'll be good. I'll do my best.

00:09:10.447 --> 00:09:12.199
So don't be stressed.

00:09:12.282 --> 00:09:16.870
You have to relax, sleep well,
and eat well to recover fast.

00:09:17.996 --> 00:09:21.458
Trust me. You know what I'm capable of,
once I get into it.

00:09:22.501 --> 00:09:25.420
I know. Dad used to say that.

00:09:25.504 --> 00:09:29.674
"If Ji-woo really puts her mind to it,
even ten guys couldn't take her down."

00:09:38.934 --> 00:09:40.310
-Ji-yeon.
-Yeah?

00:09:40.852 --> 00:09:41.853
Divorce him.

00:09:43.605 --> 00:09:44.606
Not yet.

00:09:44.689 --> 00:09:46.525
How can you see that face every day?

00:09:46.608 --> 00:09:49.611
I have no official reason
to divorce him yet.

00:09:50.695 --> 00:09:53.448
He's such a diligent and sweet husband
on the outside.

00:09:54.533 --> 00:09:55.700
So I'm waiting.

00:09:56.243 --> 00:10:00.330
If I continue to drive him
into a corner, he'll fall.

00:10:04.876 --> 00:10:06.503
INCOMING CALL
LEE KYEONG-DO

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:16.680
Don't blame Kyeong-do too much.

00:10:17.514 --> 00:10:19.266
It was me who insisted.

00:10:19.349 --> 00:10:22.561
I asked him not to say anything to you
until I tell you first.

00:10:23.645 --> 00:10:25.730
I'm sure he was stressed about it too.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:38.827
INCOMING CALL
MR. KIM

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:40.078
Yes, Mr. Kim.

00:10:40.162 --> 00:10:42.581
Ji-woo must be sleeping.
The lights are off.

00:10:42.664 --> 00:10:45.000
Maybe she's drinking? Shall I go check?

00:10:45.083 --> 00:10:48.253
Ji-yeon was already here,
so she'll be fine.

00:10:48.336 --> 00:10:50.422
You can relax and get some sleep.

00:10:52.632 --> 00:10:53.758
Okay. Thank you.

00:10:53.842 --> 00:10:56.344
No, I was here because I was worried.

00:10:56.428 --> 00:10:58.305
-Bye now.
-Bye.

00:11:09.774 --> 00:11:11.860
EPISODE 10

00:11:17.282 --> 00:11:19.117
-Assistant Manager Lee.
-Yes.

00:11:20.619 --> 00:11:22.871
Are things not going well in your life?

00:11:24.956 --> 00:11:25.790
Everything's fine.

00:11:25.874 --> 00:11:28.210
-You look completely run-down.
-No, I don't.

00:11:28.293 --> 00:11:29.336
Hey,

00:11:30.545 --> 00:11:32.797
come try tarot reading with me.
I found a place.

00:11:32.881 --> 00:11:34.090
Good. Enjoy.

00:11:34.174 --> 00:11:35.592
I'm interested.

00:11:36.218 --> 00:11:38.970
Forget it. What does a rich boy
have to worry about?

00:11:39.513 --> 00:11:40.847
Come on…

00:11:43.767 --> 00:11:44.851
Assistant Manager,

00:11:45.519 --> 00:11:46.394
a coffee?

00:11:49.105 --> 00:11:50.190
Sure. Yes.

00:11:52.359 --> 00:11:54.653
Kyeong-do, I got a call from An Da-hye.

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:56.404
What did she say?

00:11:56.488 --> 00:11:59.658
That she has a question and wants to meet.
I'm so nervous.

00:11:59.741 --> 00:12:00.867
Schedule a visit. Let's go.

00:12:00.951 --> 00:12:02.369
I'll do it, but you go in alone.

00:12:03.245 --> 00:12:04.621
She'd be upset and say nothing.

00:12:04.704 --> 00:12:06.122
But I'm scared.

00:12:06.831 --> 00:12:10.460
Hey, I heard it was a mess. Right?
Damn it.

00:12:10.544 --> 00:12:12.003
What are you doing here?

00:12:12.087 --> 00:12:16.508
So bitter. Hey, add some sweeteners.
Jeez, how many shots did you add to it?

00:12:16.591 --> 00:12:18.635
Pain, pain, pain in the ass you are.

00:12:18.718 --> 00:12:20.637
Wait, what do you mean? What mess?

00:12:21.429 --> 00:12:23.974
JARIM. Your girlfriend's company.

00:12:24.057 --> 00:12:25.475
-Just drink this.
-Hey.

00:12:25.559 --> 00:12:27.185
I'm only checking the facts.

00:12:29.104 --> 00:12:30.355
Are you writing about it?

00:12:30.438 --> 00:12:31.439
What is it?

00:12:32.315 --> 00:12:33.191
What's going on?

00:12:33.275 --> 00:12:34.901
Hey, get out and get back to work.

00:12:34.985 --> 00:12:36.027
You always leave me out.

00:12:36.111 --> 00:12:37.779
The elders are talking. Get out.

00:12:37.862 --> 00:12:39.197
-What…
-Now!

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:42.200
Okay, jeez.

00:12:47.122 --> 00:12:48.665
Okay.

00:12:49.541 --> 00:12:52.544
Before you write about it,
interview CEO Seo's doctor first.

00:12:53.628 --> 00:12:54.629
So it's dementia?

00:12:54.713 --> 00:12:57.382
I'll schedule an interview for you.
Get your facts straight.

00:12:58.049 --> 00:13:02.178
You're acting like their son-in-law,
arranging a meeting with their doctor?

00:13:02.262 --> 00:13:03.888
Hey, I'm not joking.

00:13:03.972 --> 00:13:05.015
Okay, I heard you.

00:13:06.182 --> 00:13:09.978
If this turns out well,
get me a job in the JARIM PR Team.

00:13:10.061 --> 00:13:12.063
I'd be good at writing press releases.

00:13:12.731 --> 00:13:14.899
You're out of your freaking mind.

00:13:14.983 --> 00:13:16.860
Hey. Look, Mr. Lee.

00:13:16.943 --> 00:13:21.615
Wait for me. Aren't you temperamental.
Mr. Lee!

00:13:21.698 --> 00:13:26.119
It's a relief that you're doing well
in the company after joining.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:28.538
I still have a long way to go.

00:13:29.372 --> 00:13:32.000
Did you talk to your sister yesterday?
What did she say?

00:13:34.252 --> 00:13:35.462
Be careful.

00:13:36.838 --> 00:13:39.007
Act like you don't know anything yet.

00:13:39.633 --> 00:13:41.509
She told me not to worry about her

00:13:41.593 --> 00:13:44.346
and focus on the company,
consulting you if needed.

00:13:45.096 --> 00:13:48.475
I told her to rest.
What's so important about the company?

00:13:48.558 --> 00:13:49.559
I know.

00:13:50.602 --> 00:13:53.104
What about Lucas? How are things going?

00:13:54.481 --> 00:13:55.815
It's noisy in the company.

00:13:55.899 --> 00:13:59.319
It won't settle until we have good energy.

00:14:01.279 --> 00:14:04.866
The executives are murmuring about her.

00:14:04.949 --> 00:14:07.077
If JARIM becomes dirt cheap
even before we know it…

00:14:08.078 --> 00:14:11.748
Kang Min-woo has been planning
to sell the company for a long time.

00:14:13.291 --> 00:14:15.418
He was the one
who informed about Cho Jin-eon.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:18.171
That's what I'm worried about too.

00:14:19.381 --> 00:14:22.217
It's not like I have any power.

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:24.636
They give me looks
since I'm known as the troublemaker.

00:14:25.887 --> 00:14:27.514
I need your help, Min-woo.

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:30.308
We need to protect the company.

00:14:31.393 --> 00:14:32.769
No need to mention it.

00:14:32.852 --> 00:14:37.107
Anyway, don't worry too much, Ji-woo.

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:38.441
Keep calm, okay?

00:14:39.484 --> 00:14:40.318
Yes.

00:14:41.736 --> 00:14:46.282
If we bring Ro-a back,
wouldn't that help Ji-yeon relax?

00:14:47.534 --> 00:14:49.953
There are good international schools
here too.

00:14:50.787 --> 00:14:53.123
If Ro-a stays close to her, Ji-yeon will--

00:14:53.206 --> 00:14:54.290
You've matured.

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:02.298
If you'd been like this sooner,
your sister wouldn't have been so stressed

00:15:02.382 --> 00:15:03.591
and felt supported.

00:15:07.137 --> 00:15:09.806
Better late than never. It's a good thing.

00:15:16.354 --> 00:15:17.856
Sunny days come indeed.

00:15:20.024 --> 00:15:21.693
My father-in-law would be happy.

00:15:57.687 --> 00:15:59.272
INCOMING CALL
LEE KYEONG-DO

00:16:04.903 --> 00:16:06.112
MISSED CALL
LEE KYEONG-DO

00:16:21.336 --> 00:16:25.006
INCOMING CALL
LEE KYEONG-DO

00:16:26.966 --> 00:16:27.967
Yes.

00:16:29.636 --> 00:16:31.846
What about dinner? Have you eaten?

00:16:33.181 --> 00:16:34.224
Just a little.

00:16:36.059 --> 00:16:36.893
What about you?

00:16:38.228 --> 00:16:39.312
Me too.

00:16:46.778 --> 00:16:48.446
Are you disappointed in me?

00:16:51.533 --> 00:16:53.785
I can't describe what I'm feeling.

00:16:56.788 --> 00:16:59.999
I'm thankful but frustrated.

00:17:04.671 --> 00:17:05.755
Sorry.

00:17:14.556 --> 00:17:15.849
Where are you?

00:17:19.978 --> 00:17:21.354
Here.

00:17:46.546 --> 00:17:49.507
You're getting skinny.
You're skipping meals.

00:17:50.758 --> 00:17:52.176
How long have you been there?

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:54.804
For some time after I got off work.

00:18:00.226 --> 00:18:01.853
Kyeong-do.

00:18:02.937 --> 00:18:07.150
I don't know what this feeling is.

00:18:08.818 --> 00:18:12.989
You protected my sister for me
when I was wandering.

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.828
But why did the incident at the airport
come to my mind, so selfishly?

00:18:21.789 --> 00:18:25.376
"Maybe Kyeong-do didn't stop me for love."

00:18:26.878 --> 00:18:29.172
"Was he forced because Ji-yeon asked him?"

00:18:31.257 --> 00:18:34.510
This is no time to think about that.

00:18:36.346 --> 00:18:39.307
Aren't I so selfish?

00:18:40.808 --> 00:18:43.436
To have those thoughts?

00:18:46.189 --> 00:18:47.857
You know what, Ji-woo?

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:53.363
When I went to meet you at the airport,
I was thinking,

00:18:56.449 --> 00:18:58.576
"Ji-woo's sister's illness

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:01.329
is giving me an excuse."

00:19:02.205 --> 00:19:05.124
Otherwise, I didn't have
any other excuse to stop you.

00:19:05.208 --> 00:19:07.752
"I have no choice but to stop Seo Ji-woo."

00:19:09.295 --> 00:19:12.006
Aren't I damn selfish
to have that thought?

00:19:13.508 --> 00:19:15.677
But at the time, nothing mattered.

00:19:16.302 --> 00:19:18.262
"Only if you don't leave."

00:19:20.098 --> 00:19:22.016
"Now that you're single again..."

00:19:23.601 --> 00:19:25.311
"Only if you stay close to me."

00:19:28.648 --> 00:19:30.483
That's all I could think about.

00:19:34.278 --> 00:19:35.989
If that's not love,

00:19:37.365 --> 00:19:38.533
what is?

00:19:43.538 --> 00:19:44.956
Hold me.

00:20:16.988 --> 00:20:18.322
I was scared.

00:20:20.867 --> 00:20:22.201
You have me.

00:20:24.579 --> 00:20:25.913
I'm right here.

00:20:57.445 --> 00:21:00.448
I'm only performing on weekdays.

00:21:00.531 --> 00:21:02.617
It's a big theater.

00:21:03.576 --> 00:21:07.789
My goodness.
Playing the lead role in such a big show?

00:21:09.415 --> 00:21:11.250
My Cha Woo-sik is playing the lead role?

00:21:11.334 --> 00:21:15.546
Three people are taking turns to perform,
and I just do once or twice a week.

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:18.466
Still, it's a lead role.

00:21:18.549 --> 00:21:21.344
Being kind pays off.

00:21:22.178 --> 00:21:23.763
You're finally getting paid.

00:21:25.807 --> 00:21:28.434
That reminds me. The pay.

00:21:28.518 --> 00:21:30.645
Playing Godot should pay a lot.

00:21:31.354 --> 00:21:33.147
Let's get a new bed for Dong-won.

00:21:34.774 --> 00:21:36.651
What about the money you got
for painting Ji-woo?

00:21:36.734 --> 00:21:39.654
I bought your mother a necklace with that.
Ten don of pure gold.

00:21:39.737 --> 00:21:43.032
Her friends are wearing something heavy
or whatever.

00:21:43.116 --> 00:21:45.243
She even gave us a building.

00:21:45.326 --> 00:21:48.287
I can do that for her.
That's the kind of daughter-in-law I am.

00:21:48.371 --> 00:21:49.288
Right.

00:21:52.041 --> 00:21:53.334
Why won't it come off?

00:21:56.295 --> 00:21:59.715
Woo-sik. Cha Woo-sik?

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:02.176
Is it gone?

00:22:03.511 --> 00:22:04.554
Did you spend it all?

00:22:06.430 --> 00:22:08.975
When you're a father and a breadwinner?

00:22:09.684 --> 00:22:10.852
Well…

00:22:12.145 --> 00:22:15.898
Se-yeong, there was something
I really wanted.

00:22:15.982 --> 00:22:16.816
So I bought it.

00:22:19.485 --> 00:22:20.820
What did you buy?

00:22:22.238 --> 00:22:23.281
Something on home shopping.

00:22:26.325 --> 00:22:28.661
Did you buy the TV in the end?

00:22:28.744 --> 00:22:31.747
Wait. No. Wait. That's not it. Wait.

00:22:31.831 --> 00:22:34.125
Wait. Give me a second. Let me find it.

00:22:37.962 --> 00:22:39.755
What is it?

00:22:39.839 --> 00:22:42.884
DA NANG FAMILY PACKAGE TOUR
5 NIGHTS 7 DAYS SPECIAL PRICE

00:22:42.967 --> 00:22:44.635
-Vietnam?
-It's just…

00:22:44.719 --> 00:22:48.222
I mean, we should travel abroad too, no?

00:22:48.306 --> 00:22:52.185
This building came with the loan,
so you had such a hard time paying it off.

00:22:52.268 --> 00:22:56.230
I worked part-time doing delivery and all
and never brought a decent paycheck.

00:22:56.314 --> 00:22:58.149
Our poor Dong-won.

00:22:58.232 --> 00:23:01.235
Let's give him a chance
to take a passport photo this time.

00:23:11.412 --> 00:23:12.246
Se-yeong?

00:23:13.831 --> 00:23:16.209
I'm sorry. Don't cry.
This is all my fault.

00:23:16.292 --> 00:23:19.503
I'll cancel it. I can get a refund.
I swear I can have my money back, okay?

00:23:22.256 --> 00:23:23.257
Honey!

00:23:23.341 --> 00:23:24.342
Yes.

00:23:25.259 --> 00:23:26.886
Good job!

00:23:28.554 --> 00:23:30.097
Thank you!

00:23:30.181 --> 00:23:33.309
This is why I love you.

00:23:33.392 --> 00:23:35.645
You're so cool.

00:23:35.728 --> 00:23:37.855
Oh, gosh, Se-yeong. Thank you so much.

00:23:37.939 --> 00:23:41.901
I mean, it's not refundable,
so I was so scared.

00:23:41.984 --> 00:23:43.945
-I was worried to death.
-Dong-won.

00:23:44.028 --> 00:23:46.197
Dong-won, come here.

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:49.283
-Dong-won.
-My baby.

00:23:49.367 --> 00:23:52.078
-Let's go travel.
-Dong-won, the passport…

00:23:52.828 --> 00:23:55.289
Why are you crying?

00:23:55.373 --> 00:23:57.375
CORRECTIONAL CENTER
MINISTRY OF JUSTICE

00:24:00.127 --> 00:24:01.295
You followed along?

00:24:01.379 --> 00:24:03.965
I have nothing to say to you, but…

00:24:04.048 --> 00:24:05.758
I have some questions.

00:24:05.841 --> 00:24:07.051
Like what?

00:24:07.134 --> 00:24:09.220
Why did you want to meet
Reporter Kim Doo-jin?

00:24:09.303 --> 00:24:11.097
Why do you want to know?

00:24:12.765 --> 00:24:13.975
You know Kang Min-woo, right?

00:24:15.226 --> 00:24:18.020
Of course.
He's Cho Jin-eon's brother-in-law.

00:24:18.104 --> 00:24:19.939
I want to know what's between you two.

00:24:22.024 --> 00:24:23.526
What does it look like to you?

00:24:25.486 --> 00:24:26.946
Let me rephrase the question.

00:24:28.197 --> 00:24:32.076
Why do you think he reported
what's between you and Cho Jin-eon?

00:24:36.247 --> 00:24:39.667
Is it okay for a reporter
to reveal the informant?

00:24:40.751 --> 00:24:43.921
I didn't know he was the informant.
I received it by mail--

00:24:44.547 --> 00:24:46.299
I found out through another route.

00:24:46.924 --> 00:24:48.092
Do you know him well?

00:24:48.718 --> 00:24:49.552
No.

00:24:50.177 --> 00:24:51.387
We've only said hi.

00:24:51.470 --> 00:24:54.181
Maybe we met once or twice.
But that's funny.

00:24:54.265 --> 00:24:57.059
Who the hell does that fucker think he is,
tipping off the press about me?

00:24:59.228 --> 00:25:01.731
If you were just curious
about the informant,

00:25:01.814 --> 00:25:03.733
then you don't need
Reporter Kim anymore, right?

00:25:06.193 --> 00:25:07.194
Reporter Lee.

00:25:07.278 --> 00:25:08.321
Yes.

00:25:08.404 --> 00:25:11.365
All I'm asking for is one thing.

00:25:11.449 --> 00:25:14.035
I can't wait to get out of here.

00:25:14.618 --> 00:25:17.747
Why the hell am I stuck in here
when Cho Jin-eon is on probation?

00:25:17.830 --> 00:25:19.290
I'm not the only one who did drugs.

00:25:20.082 --> 00:25:24.545
Who's going to get me out of here?
Cho Jin-eon won't answer his phone.

00:25:24.628 --> 00:25:28.049
So I thought I should find the informant
through the reporter and screw him up.

00:25:29.133 --> 00:25:30.343
But then,

00:25:31.344 --> 00:25:34.013
what could I possibly do
when I couldn't even reach him?

00:25:35.306 --> 00:25:39.018
So you knew
Kang Min-woo was the informant,

00:25:39.101 --> 00:25:40.770
and you needed Reporter Kim to confirm.

00:25:41.812 --> 00:25:45.024
Oh my. Is that what I said?

00:25:48.027 --> 00:25:53.115
The reporters always catch me so easily.
Even in my prime.

00:25:53.199 --> 00:25:56.744
You already contacted Kang Min-woo,
but he's not answering.

00:26:00.206 --> 00:26:01.624
What do you want to know?

00:26:03.376 --> 00:26:06.087
Why would you want
to screw Kang Min-woo up?

00:26:08.047 --> 00:26:11.425
The reason you chose him
as the rope to get you out of here,

00:26:12.176 --> 00:26:15.304
the dangerous reason for him to do that...
That's what I want.

00:26:21.435 --> 00:26:25.606
There is no dangerous reason to do that,
Reporter Lee.

00:26:26.565 --> 00:26:27.608
Let's say there is.

00:26:27.691 --> 00:26:32.113
Like a movie, let's say there is.

00:26:33.072 --> 00:26:36.659
Then are you going to save me
instead of Kang Min-woo?

00:26:39.453 --> 00:26:42.206
The court will sentence you
according to the law.

00:26:44.458 --> 00:26:46.544
You have nothing.

00:26:47.378 --> 00:26:49.880
You have no power. You have no backup.

00:26:51.173 --> 00:26:53.175
Unless you have a good card, don't come.

00:26:53.801 --> 00:26:56.512
I also have a routine.

00:26:56.595 --> 00:27:00.099
It's hard to kill each day
of my sentence in here.

00:27:05.354 --> 00:27:06.355
Didroxin.

00:27:10.025 --> 00:27:11.694
Kang Min-woo will react to that.

00:27:14.196 --> 00:27:18.909
Didroxin? So is that a button
that will trigger Kang Min-woo?

00:27:31.755 --> 00:27:33.924
It began with the article I wrote.

00:27:34.008 --> 00:27:35.968
"JARIM CEO's Alzheimer's…"

00:27:36.886 --> 00:27:38.471
It's not Alzheimer's.

00:27:38.554 --> 00:27:41.307
Kyeong-do, this is quite serious.

00:27:43.017 --> 00:27:44.310
How far are you planning to go?

00:27:44.393 --> 00:27:47.771
Where that asshole is going.
I have to be there first.

00:27:50.608 --> 00:27:51.775
ECONOMICS TEAM
MA SUNG-CHEOL

00:27:52.985 --> 00:27:54.195
Hey.

00:27:54.278 --> 00:27:55.946
Hey, did you read the article?

00:27:56.030 --> 00:27:59.366
I was working. I'll read it soon.
Did you make it good?

00:27:59.450 --> 00:28:02.703
You're not even my department manager.
How dare you check--

00:28:02.786 --> 00:28:03.996
-Find the article.
-Okay.

00:28:05.372 --> 00:28:08.125
JARIM CEO SEO JI-YEON

00:28:10.044 --> 00:28:13.130
'DIDROXIN'S TEMPORARY SIDE EFFECT'
NO ISSUE IN MANAGEMENT

00:28:15.424 --> 00:28:18.511
'DIDROXIN'S TEMPORARY SIDE EFFECT'
NO ISSUE IN MANAGEMENT

00:28:22.139 --> 00:28:23.140
Dementia?

00:28:24.517 --> 00:28:27.019
If you take Didroxin wrong,
you get dementia?

00:28:29.021 --> 00:28:31.065
Yes. Right.

00:28:33.275 --> 00:28:34.401
Seo Ji-yeon?

00:28:35.444 --> 00:28:36.695
From JARIM Apparel?

00:28:40.533 --> 00:28:41.784
No shit.

00:28:43.869 --> 00:28:46.872
He's one hell of an asshole. Listen.

00:28:47.790 --> 00:28:50.668
Send him one more quick delivery.
This time, put it as…

00:28:53.003 --> 00:28:56.590
"Didroxin, a visit requested."

00:28:57.341 --> 00:28:58.342
As simple as that.

00:29:07.726 --> 00:29:12.898
Yoo Dan-bi didn't post it herself.
Her friend posted it, and she tagged her.

00:29:13.524 --> 00:29:16.402
Compared to last year,
the budget on her posts is different.

00:29:16.485 --> 00:29:17.903
She obviously has more money.

00:29:19.905 --> 00:29:21.240
Anything else that stands out?

00:29:21.323 --> 00:29:25.077
Well, it seems she's posting
less than before.

00:29:25.160 --> 00:29:27.079
She's clearly aware of something.

00:29:27.746 --> 00:29:28.998
How about her routine after work?

00:29:29.081 --> 00:29:31.166
She's really into Pilates.

00:29:31.792 --> 00:29:34.295
But she always has a drink
after her class.

00:29:34.378 --> 00:29:36.422
Then what's the point of all that?

00:29:36.505 --> 00:29:38.674
She goes to her regular places
on a random basis.

00:29:38.757 --> 00:29:40.259
-By herself?
-No.

00:29:40.342 --> 00:29:42.553
She's an insider.
With new faces almost every time.

00:30:16.712 --> 00:30:17.713
Here.

00:30:19.173 --> 00:30:21.425
Eat. When you have low sugar,
you have no energy.

00:30:24.053 --> 00:30:27.389
But don't you think this is wrong
at ten o'clock at night?

00:30:27.473 --> 00:30:30.976
Eat with a sense of duty
as if JARIM's future relies on your arms.

00:30:34.396 --> 00:30:35.397
Here.

00:30:38.942 --> 00:30:39.777
Good girl.

00:30:44.406 --> 00:30:46.867
How's Ji-yeon doing?

00:30:48.577 --> 00:30:51.246
Mother, you don't need to worry too much.

00:30:51.330 --> 00:30:54.875
Ji-yeon is the same as usual.
You've read the article.

00:30:55.709 --> 00:30:57.586
The illness doesn't get that serious.

00:30:59.588 --> 00:31:01.632
How's the atmosphere at work?

00:31:02.591 --> 00:31:06.929
The noise died down when we said
it was the side effect of a drug.

00:31:08.597 --> 00:31:10.641
Only you're still sensitive about it.

00:31:11.934 --> 00:31:13.477
It'll make you ill.

00:31:15.521 --> 00:31:17.147
Excuse me. Let me make a quick call.

00:31:17.231 --> 00:31:18.273
Yes, go ahead.

00:31:57.187 --> 00:31:59.189
Hey. When did you get here?

00:32:00.357 --> 00:32:01.358
Just now.

00:32:02.359 --> 00:32:04.611
What were you doing in Mom's room?

00:32:04.695 --> 00:32:08.824
Well, I was wondering
if we had to change her bathroom tiles.

00:32:09.616 --> 00:32:11.076
She said they were slippery.

00:32:12.745 --> 00:32:13.579
Did she?

00:32:13.662 --> 00:32:17.291
How come you pay less attention than me
when you're her daughter? Let's go.

00:32:17.374 --> 00:32:18.500
Go ahead.

00:32:18.584 --> 00:32:20.002
I'm here with Ji-woo.

00:32:20.919 --> 00:32:24.673
Ji-woo too? Hurry up.
I have a meeting, so I have to get going.

00:32:24.757 --> 00:32:25.758
Okay.

00:32:54.286 --> 00:32:57.331
I was going to keep it
between Ji-woo and me until I settle it.

00:33:00.334 --> 00:33:02.211
What has this man done to you?

00:33:03.295 --> 00:33:04.546
Before that…

00:33:06.048 --> 00:33:07.758
I think he is going to...

00:33:09.885 --> 00:33:11.804
disclose our mother-daughter story.

00:33:12.888 --> 00:33:13.722
What story?

00:33:15.390 --> 00:33:16.391
About Ji-woo?

00:33:17.976 --> 00:33:19.394
That she's not Dad's biological child?

00:33:20.145 --> 00:33:21.480
He's going to disclose that?

00:33:23.649 --> 00:33:24.650
I think so.

00:33:28.362 --> 00:33:30.405
We might as well get ready for it.

00:33:31.114 --> 00:33:33.075
Why is he going that far?

00:33:35.869 --> 00:33:37.788
I end up

00:33:39.289 --> 00:33:41.875
tying you down.

00:33:54.847 --> 00:33:58.350
How can you sue me? I'm hurt.

00:33:59.142 --> 00:34:00.143
Min-woo,

00:34:01.019 --> 00:34:04.857
buying and selling JARIM requires
a lot more than buying a corner store.

00:34:04.940 --> 00:34:06.108
Right.

00:34:06.191 --> 00:34:08.527
Nothing guarantees
that Aaron invests it in JARIM.

00:34:08.610 --> 00:34:09.736
I know.

00:34:09.820 --> 00:34:11.405
Then why do you keep putting it off?

00:34:12.114 --> 00:34:15.075
You show no action.
I need to find a way to live as well.

00:34:15.742 --> 00:34:18.662
You think 30 billion won is a joke?

00:34:18.745 --> 00:34:22.082
The stock market's fluctuating
because Seo Ji-woo recruited Lucas.

00:34:22.165 --> 00:34:23.792
JARIM will never be for sale.

00:34:24.751 --> 00:34:26.253
You're right.

00:34:27.254 --> 00:34:28.839
I never thought Seo Ji-woo would help.

00:34:30.090 --> 00:34:31.466
-Min-woo.
-Jun-soo.

00:34:32.134 --> 00:34:33.135
Bae Jun-soo.

00:34:35.429 --> 00:34:39.850
The stock market is fluctuating.
JARIM's value went up.

00:34:39.933 --> 00:34:42.936
So if it's on the market,
everyone will be eager to buy it.

00:34:43.562 --> 00:34:45.772
Even without Aaron's fund,
people will bite it.

00:34:47.107 --> 00:34:50.736
Then you need to butter me up,
not fucking sue me.

00:34:53.697 --> 00:34:57.034
Are you sure it's even on the market?
Does Seo Ji-yeon agree to sell it?

00:34:57.117 --> 00:34:58.952
She's not going to, obviously.

00:35:00.120 --> 00:35:02.706
I'll have to make her agree to it!

00:35:02.789 --> 00:35:04.625
I'm busy working on that,

00:35:04.708 --> 00:35:07.586
that's why I'm having fucking raw fish
instead of a proper meal!

00:35:16.803 --> 00:35:19.890
Seo Ji-woo,
she's not Chairman Seo's daughter.

00:35:21.642 --> 00:35:24.353
I was busy
sending the DNA test today, buddy.

00:35:25.938 --> 00:35:29.524
Seo Ji-yeon's dementia,
Seo Ji-woo being an illegitimate child...

00:35:29.608 --> 00:35:31.777
That creates a management risk.

00:35:31.860 --> 00:35:33.737
I talked to Executive Director Choi.

00:35:33.820 --> 00:35:36.740
Once the article on Ji-woo is released,

00:35:36.823 --> 00:35:39.910
Seo Ji-woo will be kicked out.
Then Seo Ji-yeon will stagger.

00:35:39.993 --> 00:35:43.080
Whatever Seo Ji-yeon says,
you think people will listen?

00:35:50.045 --> 00:35:53.799
But how can you do the DNA test
when your father's deceased? Are you sure?

00:35:55.050 --> 00:35:59.429
I looked it up.
A DNA test of the sisters and the mother

00:35:59.513 --> 00:36:01.348
shows that they have different fathers.

00:36:09.314 --> 00:36:13.193
I'm okay, but I'm worried about Mom.

00:36:13.276 --> 00:36:15.404
The company would come after me too.

00:36:18.365 --> 00:36:19.741
Are you sure you'll be okay?

00:36:21.326 --> 00:36:23.286
Yes. Well…

00:36:24.079 --> 00:36:26.957
My phone will be on fire,
and I'll be bombarded with texts.

00:36:27.833 --> 00:36:29.960
Like when my divorce news got out.

00:36:31.378 --> 00:36:33.380
It'll get quiet after some time.

00:36:39.803 --> 00:36:42.305
Kang Min-woo won't let this slide.

00:36:44.433 --> 00:36:45.767
Let's get ahead of him.

00:36:46.601 --> 00:36:48.562
I swear Kang Min-woo will play a game.

00:36:48.645 --> 00:36:51.314
And if it's going to happen,
whoever plays it first wins.

00:36:53.066 --> 00:36:54.860
But then you…

00:37:04.036 --> 00:37:05.662
You're smart.

00:37:06.329 --> 00:37:08.415
You did earn the Assistant Manager title.

00:37:23.138 --> 00:37:24.431
Sit down.

00:37:25.849 --> 00:37:27.976
Let me just borrow a pen.

00:37:28.060 --> 00:37:29.686
-Hey, that's mine.
-Come on.

00:37:29.770 --> 00:37:31.063
Let me use it just this once…

00:37:34.900 --> 00:37:36.151
Hey, you're here.

00:37:37.903 --> 00:37:39.279
Hello.

00:37:40.405 --> 00:37:43.325
Have you had coffee yet?
We also have Job's tears tea.

00:37:44.910 --> 00:37:46.703
Coffee, please. Iced.

00:37:47.746 --> 00:37:49.581
Assistant Manager Lee.
Two iced Americanos.

00:37:50.499 --> 00:37:51.583
Come with me.

00:37:52.959 --> 00:37:54.336
-Three iced Americanos.
-What?

00:37:54.419 --> 00:37:56.755
-First time visiting a press company?
-Yes, it's interesting.

00:37:56.838 --> 00:37:59.758
The Entertainment Team
is at the end of the hall.

00:37:59.841 --> 00:38:02.427
This is the Politics Team.
The Current Affairs Team's there.

00:38:02.511 --> 00:38:04.012
This way.

00:38:10.268 --> 00:38:12.646
-But…
-That means, "Know when to join."

00:38:12.729 --> 00:38:13.939
Aren't you getting coffee?

00:38:14.022 --> 00:38:15.440
Yes, sir.

00:38:16.608 --> 00:38:18.026
But why…

00:38:19.402 --> 00:38:21.988
Wait. What?

00:38:24.324 --> 00:38:26.034
Gosh…

00:38:26.118 --> 00:38:30.122
I'd like you to write the article.

00:38:30.205 --> 00:38:31.331
Me?

00:38:31.414 --> 00:38:35.293
The temperature of your words
would be different.

00:38:36.169 --> 00:38:38.421
Being not so fond of me
is also a sign of interest.

00:38:45.262 --> 00:38:49.182
In a way it would induce sympathy, please.

00:38:52.102 --> 00:38:53.937
People wouldn't pity you for that.

00:38:56.148 --> 00:38:59.818
Just show yourself as you are.

00:39:01.695 --> 00:39:04.114
Just as I am?

00:39:04.739 --> 00:39:05.782
Yes.

00:39:10.537 --> 00:39:12.998
Sounds good.
Please write it as a special article.

00:39:13.707 --> 00:39:16.084
A couple of photos on it would be better.

00:39:16.168 --> 00:39:18.712
Okay, sure. In terms of the photos…

00:39:18.795 --> 00:39:21.798
You're not using random photos
on the internet…

00:39:21.882 --> 00:39:24.426
are you?

00:39:29.556 --> 00:39:32.100
What is he, a dog that needs to poop?
Damn it.

00:39:34.269 --> 00:39:35.604
I'll find a photographer.

00:39:35.687 --> 00:39:37.105
I can do it today.

00:39:37.189 --> 00:39:40.066
Would you like to go to the salon?
It'll take some time.

00:39:40.150 --> 00:39:41.276
Sure, thank you.

00:39:41.359 --> 00:39:44.279
Thank you. For giving us an article.

00:39:45.363 --> 00:39:47.699
You'll get explosive views for sure.

00:39:49.367 --> 00:39:51.536
An illegitimate child out of wedlock.

00:39:53.205 --> 00:39:54.247
It's a nice keyword.

00:39:57.584 --> 00:39:58.501
I'll see you later.

00:39:58.585 --> 00:40:00.170
Yes, sure.

00:40:02.339 --> 00:40:04.257
Take care. I'll see you later.

00:40:04.341 --> 00:40:06.218
Bye. Thank you for the coffee.

00:40:16.144 --> 00:40:18.104
So you'd just meet her directly?

00:40:18.188 --> 00:40:20.315
It's too big for a mere assistant manager.

00:40:21.566 --> 00:40:24.486
Hey. I'm the legend
of Dongwoon Daily's Entertainment Team.

00:40:24.569 --> 00:40:26.780
Says who?

00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:40.502
Why is she smiling like that?

00:41:04.526 --> 00:41:07.946
Wait, this is good. I like the third one.

00:41:09.281 --> 00:41:10.615
It's perfect with the breeze.

00:41:15.453 --> 00:41:16.496
My goodness.

00:41:17.831 --> 00:41:18.999
Even like that, she's pretty.

00:41:21.418 --> 00:41:23.003
So brazenly pretty.

00:41:29.718 --> 00:41:32.762
When did you first find out about that?

00:41:33.346 --> 00:41:34.597
I was 28.

00:41:34.681 --> 00:41:36.891
And you hadn't noticed it until then?

00:41:36.975 --> 00:41:37.976
No.

00:41:39.185 --> 00:41:40.979
That's how my father was.

00:41:41.688 --> 00:41:45.900
Perhaps, he loved me more than my sister.

00:41:46.776 --> 00:41:50.488
When you found out,
you must've had a lot on your mind.

00:41:51.531 --> 00:41:53.033
A lot…

00:41:55.201 --> 00:41:58.246
I did have a lot on my mind.

00:41:58.330 --> 00:42:02.500
How should I put it?
Should I say I seemed ridiculous?

00:42:02.584 --> 00:42:05.837
I didn't deserve everything
I took for granted.

00:42:05.920 --> 00:42:08.173
That sense of self-destruction.

00:42:09.049 --> 00:42:13.386
Everything around me,
the people and the environment...

00:42:13.470 --> 00:42:16.639
I became ashamed toward them all.

00:42:19.267 --> 00:42:21.770
So back then, I ran away.

00:42:22.520 --> 00:42:23.980
From everything.

00:42:24.689 --> 00:42:29.444
Ever since then, have you talked
to your father, mother, or your sister?

00:42:30.570 --> 00:42:31.696
No.

00:42:31.780 --> 00:42:34.574
When I was running away to the US,

00:42:34.657 --> 00:42:37.702
my father and I talked
about this and that at the airport.

00:42:38.286 --> 00:42:42.999
Though we were talking about other things,
the message was "thank you",

00:42:44.042 --> 00:42:46.252
"I love you" and "I appreciate you".

00:42:48.338 --> 00:42:51.925
It's only very recently
that I had the talk with my mother.

00:42:53.510 --> 00:42:54.719
This interview,

00:42:54.803 --> 00:42:59.182
it must have not been an easy decision,
not only for you, but for her as well.

00:42:59.724 --> 00:43:01.101
Yet she still agreed to it.

00:43:03.645 --> 00:43:07.148
If you say no, I won't do it.

00:43:07.982 --> 00:43:09.859
It'll be out anyway.

00:43:11.736 --> 00:43:13.655
Kang Min-woo, that man,

00:43:14.656 --> 00:43:16.324
even had the DNA test done.

00:43:18.159 --> 00:43:20.537
Although this is my doing,

00:43:23.248 --> 00:43:24.791
how can I live with that?

00:43:26.543 --> 00:43:28.962
How am I going to live with my head up?

00:43:30.964 --> 00:43:32.507
But…

00:43:33.925 --> 00:43:36.845
it was hard on me.

00:43:39.055 --> 00:43:40.890
I had such a hard time back then.

00:43:42.142 --> 00:43:46.020
Your dad was so crazy about work
that I barely saw him.

00:43:46.104 --> 00:43:50.483
I was stuck in a house as big as a palace.
I could barely eat.

00:43:51.192 --> 00:43:53.069
I felt like dying.

00:43:54.529 --> 00:43:57.323
I didn't run away to Paris to do that.

00:43:57.407 --> 00:44:00.452
While I was living there, it just…

00:44:01.578 --> 00:44:02.704
It happened…

00:44:21.264 --> 00:44:22.265
You know what?

00:44:26.394 --> 00:44:28.521
What tortured me was…

00:44:30.940 --> 00:44:32.775
not your choice.

00:44:36.404 --> 00:44:39.657
It was that you turned your guilt
into blame toward me.

00:44:42.994 --> 00:44:45.371
I was completely in the dark.

00:44:48.124 --> 00:44:50.168
And you hated me…

00:44:50.919 --> 00:44:52.587
so much…

00:45:00.053 --> 00:45:02.013
That's what tortured me.

00:45:14.943 --> 00:45:16.194
My life,

00:45:17.612 --> 00:45:19.405
it's coming to a close.

00:45:23.159 --> 00:45:24.160
But you…

00:45:25.119 --> 00:45:26.412
Are you going to be okay?

00:45:28.748 --> 00:45:29.749
Yes.

00:45:31.793 --> 00:45:34.337
It won't be so effective.

00:45:36.589 --> 00:45:39.717
Because I've never been okay.

00:45:44.347 --> 00:45:47.809
Perhaps, you could've kept it a secret
within your family.

00:45:47.892 --> 00:45:51.312
I'd like to ask you the reason
you accepted this interview.

00:45:52.105 --> 00:45:54.440
Before my father passed away,

00:45:54.524 --> 00:45:57.485
he always wanted me to help him
with the company work.

00:45:58.236 --> 00:46:02.574
I thought it would be shameless of me,
so I kept running away from it.

00:46:03.366 --> 00:46:07.620
But now, it's time to help my sister,
CEO Seo Ji-yeon.

00:46:07.704 --> 00:46:13.585
And working hard for JARIM Apparel
is a way to repay his kindness.

00:46:14.586 --> 00:46:19.424
Revealing and explaining my situation
would be the start of all that.

00:46:21.551 --> 00:46:22.552
Very well.

00:46:30.393 --> 00:46:32.520
HER FATHER
WHO RAISED HER WITH HEART

00:46:32.604 --> 00:46:34.606
FOCUSING ON JARIM TO REPAY FATHER'S LOVE

00:46:34.689 --> 00:46:36.316
LATE CHAIRMAN'S LOVE, JARIM'S ROOT

00:46:39.444 --> 00:46:42.196
THIS IS A NEW SIDE OF SEO JI-WOO
BUT IT'S STILL SHOCKING!

00:46:48.036 --> 00:46:52.665
SHE SOUNDS RELIABLE LOL - SHE'S HONEST
LOOKING FORWARD TO SEO JI-WOO'S PATH

00:46:58.421 --> 00:47:00.423
JARIM'S SECOND DAUGHTER
THE SECRET OF HER BIRTH

00:47:04.844 --> 00:47:09.140
DNA EVALUATION - SUSPECTED
TO NOT SHARE A BIOLOGICAL FATHER

00:47:13.269 --> 00:47:14.896
She's playing smart.

00:47:28.159 --> 00:47:29.410
On vacation?

00:47:33.414 --> 00:47:36.709
They went abroad when there's an incident?

00:47:39.671 --> 00:47:41.214
Who am I supposed to have makgeolli with?

00:47:44.050 --> 00:47:45.301
Damn it.

00:47:49.847 --> 00:47:51.140
Hey, it's Kyeong-do.

00:47:51.224 --> 00:47:52.475
What?

00:47:52.558 --> 00:47:53.726
Hey, Kyeong-do,

00:47:53.810 --> 00:47:55.687
-what are you doing here?
-Hello.

00:48:03.194 --> 00:48:04.195
What's that?

00:48:04.278 --> 00:48:06.239
I knew it.

00:48:06.823 --> 00:48:09.117
You're all down, ruining your beauty.

00:48:10.034 --> 00:48:12.328
-What is that RV?
-What do you think?

00:48:12.412 --> 00:48:15.832
It's the pumpkin carriage to pick you up.
Hey, hop in.

00:48:16.999 --> 00:48:18.000
That's awesome.

00:48:18.084 --> 00:48:19.544
Mr. Kim, good night.

00:48:19.627 --> 00:48:22.046
-Ji-woo's not eaten yet. She needs to eat.
-Okay.

00:48:23.923 --> 00:48:25.591
-Goodnight.
-Drive safe.

00:48:28.052 --> 00:48:29.053
Come here.

00:48:41.023 --> 00:48:42.150
Is it your first time?

00:48:42.233 --> 00:48:45.862
Yes. Where did you get this? Whose is it?

00:48:46.779 --> 00:48:50.324
Who cares? What matters is that
we're using it right now. Just enjoy.

00:48:52.660 --> 00:48:55.872
Do you have a license for it?
Can you drive something this big?

00:48:55.955 --> 00:48:57.331
I have a license.

00:49:00.251 --> 00:49:04.046
Anyway, where are we going?
I'm dead tired.

00:49:04.130 --> 00:49:05.298
You can rest.

00:49:05.381 --> 00:49:09.343
We have a bed and a shower booth.
I'll cook. Nothing to stress about.

00:49:10.678 --> 00:49:12.972
Why are you so excited?
You didn't even come.

00:49:14.098 --> 00:49:15.892
I was busy.

00:49:15.975 --> 00:49:18.269
I bought some light to hang outside.

00:49:18.352 --> 00:49:21.981
I got stuff for the barbecue.
Tteokbokki, ramyeon, I got everything.

00:49:22.064 --> 00:49:23.691
I was busy. So busy.

00:49:41.667 --> 00:49:43.002
Can you even finish it today?

00:49:43.085 --> 00:49:44.962
No, I connected it.

00:49:45.046 --> 00:49:49.217
Maybe the light's broken.
I tested it at home, but I was in a rush.

00:49:50.134 --> 00:49:52.011
I'm hungry. Let's have ramyeon.

00:49:52.094 --> 00:49:55.848
Why have ramyeon when we have barbecue?
Ramyeon is for dessert.

00:49:55.932 --> 00:50:00.102
Sit here and get some rest.
You'll see my fire-building skill. Sit.

00:50:08.027 --> 00:50:09.737
Hey, it's burning.

00:50:11.948 --> 00:50:13.074
Or not.

00:50:14.450 --> 00:50:18.204
I feel like someone's watching me.
Maybe that's why.

00:50:23.459 --> 00:50:25.169
We can have the meat for dessert.

00:50:25.837 --> 00:50:29.423
Right. We shouldn't be so narrow-minded.

00:50:47.191 --> 00:50:50.736
I think our ancestors
came up with good proverbs.

00:50:52.446 --> 00:50:53.447
If it's to diss me, stop.

00:50:53.531 --> 00:50:57.743
"Hunger is the best side dish."
A proverb like that is so fit.

00:50:58.744 --> 00:51:01.873
"Hunger is the best side dish."
Don't you think that's poetic?

00:51:20.349 --> 00:51:22.351
The tea smells nice.

00:51:23.811 --> 00:51:26.022
It's from England. You like England.

00:51:36.866 --> 00:51:38.951
I think it's getting a little chilly--

00:51:39.035 --> 00:51:40.161
Here.

00:51:52.715 --> 00:51:53.716
Wasn't it tough?

00:51:55.593 --> 00:51:57.219
Well… It's just…

00:52:03.809 --> 00:52:06.604
Just a little. It was a little tough.

00:52:11.525 --> 00:52:12.652
You had a nice outfit.

00:52:14.153 --> 00:52:15.154
Were you there?

00:52:15.863 --> 00:52:18.574
Our Ji-woo looks great in anything.

00:52:20.493 --> 00:52:22.119
I stopped by for a second.

00:52:22.203 --> 00:52:25.081
To see how you were doing.

00:52:26.374 --> 00:52:27.625
You should've come to say hi.

00:52:32.129 --> 00:52:33.297
Because I felt bad.

00:52:34.674 --> 00:52:36.300
For asking you to do that.

00:52:37.760 --> 00:52:40.221
I felt bad, so I couldn't say hi.

00:52:42.264 --> 00:52:44.266
Idiot, why would you feel bad?

00:52:49.021 --> 00:52:50.356
I'm thankful.

00:52:55.736 --> 00:52:57.279
Thank you, Kyeong-do.

00:53:03.869 --> 00:53:04.870
I'm embarrassed.

00:53:06.455 --> 00:53:08.290
Then…

00:53:09.417 --> 00:53:10.418
how about a kiss?

00:53:16.465 --> 00:53:17.800
Shall we?

00:53:53.878 --> 00:53:55.379
Thank you.

00:54:00.843 --> 00:54:02.803
Hey, this is crazy.

00:54:05.222 --> 00:54:09.185
What would you do without me?

00:54:10.728 --> 00:54:11.562
Here.

00:54:21.238 --> 00:54:22.615
I'm still sleepy.

00:54:24.450 --> 00:54:27.870
Give me a piggyback.
I think that will wake me up.

00:54:28.662 --> 00:54:30.331
I can't do that on an empty stomach.

00:54:30.414 --> 00:54:32.124
Why not? You carried Bella Jin.

00:54:32.833 --> 00:54:34.835
That was for business.

00:54:34.919 --> 00:54:36.545
You and I,

00:54:37.505 --> 00:54:39.173
we need to cherish each other.

00:54:39.256 --> 00:54:42.426
No strength training on an empty stomach.

00:54:53.979 --> 00:54:54.980
Here we go.

00:54:59.193 --> 00:55:00.361
Nice.

00:55:07.243 --> 00:55:09.703
I think I need to stay like this
for ten more minutes.

00:55:09.787 --> 00:55:10.788
Ten minutes?

00:55:11.622 --> 00:55:12.706
Sure.

00:55:14.041 --> 00:55:16.836
Gosh, do they think
they're filming a movie?

00:55:16.919 --> 00:55:18.712
Who goes to work from here?

00:55:21.382 --> 00:55:23.134
Mr. Kim!

00:55:23.217 --> 00:55:24.426
Good morning!

00:55:24.510 --> 00:55:26.512
You're laughing? How can you be laughing?

00:55:29.598 --> 00:55:32.601
Still, Kyeong-do is the only one
who makes Ji-woo laugh.

00:55:35.604 --> 00:55:36.814
Thank you.

00:55:36.897 --> 00:55:38.566
It was nice. Thank you.

00:55:39.275 --> 00:55:41.277
What is he getting out of?

00:55:53.164 --> 00:55:56.375
Lee Kyeong-do, what's going on?
What is it?

00:55:56.458 --> 00:55:58.794
What was that RV for?

00:55:58.878 --> 00:56:00.880
Did you cover someone big?
To make me happy?

00:56:00.963 --> 00:56:05.301
No. I was just trying to see
what it's like to come to work in an RV.

00:56:05.384 --> 00:56:07.595
-You rode an RV for no reason?
-Yes.

00:56:07.678 --> 00:56:09.847
What does an RV have to do
with covering someone big?

00:56:09.930 --> 00:56:13.017
Once upon a time,
Lee Kyeong-do actually worked really hard.

00:56:14.143 --> 00:56:19.231
When Actor Ha Min-su was in his prime, no
one could cover for him. He was so busy.

00:56:19.315 --> 00:56:21.901
Then Lee Kyeong-do rented an RV.

00:56:22.860 --> 00:56:26.197
He basically kidnapped him,
giving him a ride from Seoul to Busan.

00:56:29.241 --> 00:56:32.244
Apparently, he was so touched
by Kyeong-do's effort that he said yes.

00:56:32.828 --> 00:56:36.415
What do you think he did during that time?
He gave the actor beers to gather a scoop.

00:56:38.209 --> 00:56:39.793
You and your petty tricks.

00:56:41.212 --> 00:56:43.339
Petty? Come here, you asshole.

00:56:43.422 --> 00:56:44.506
No…

00:56:44.590 --> 00:56:48.594
You know what's more amazing?
Ha Min-su bought that RV.

00:56:48.677 --> 00:56:49.720
-Exactly.
-Since then,

00:56:49.803 --> 00:56:51.972
he drove the RV to the set.

00:56:52.598 --> 00:56:55.392
Assistant Manager, you got good money
from the RV company?

00:56:56.143 --> 00:56:57.102
I'm not like you.

00:56:58.312 --> 00:57:01.106
Yet, you have nothing today?

00:57:03.734 --> 00:57:08.280
I gathered news about myself. "Who am I?"

00:57:09.156 --> 00:57:11.075
Are you shitting with your mouth?

00:57:11.659 --> 00:57:15.496
We never get along. I do respect you,
but we don't get along at all.

00:57:15.579 --> 00:57:16.914
Think again. We do get along.

00:57:16.997 --> 00:57:18.624
-We don't.
-We totally do.

00:57:18.707 --> 00:57:19.833
We totally don't.

00:57:19.917 --> 00:57:21.835
Gosh, I don't get along with any of you.

00:57:23.587 --> 00:57:25.965
The maeuntang here
is your favorite, right?

00:57:26.924 --> 00:57:28.592
My father told me.

00:57:29.301 --> 00:57:32.388
He often offered to have soju here.

00:57:33.555 --> 00:57:34.390
Give it to me.

00:57:41.981 --> 00:57:43.399
Thank you.

00:57:46.986 --> 00:57:48.070
Help yourself.

00:57:56.036 --> 00:57:57.913
No wonder you're a regular here.

00:58:03.460 --> 00:58:04.795
I assume you have something to say.

00:58:12.344 --> 00:58:13.595
I think you already know.

00:58:16.515 --> 00:58:18.976
Things are getting serious
between the executives.

00:58:19.059 --> 00:58:22.771
The employees will talk about it
and stop eventually,

00:58:22.855 --> 00:58:24.064
but the stockholders won't.

00:58:25.649 --> 00:58:30.321
The executives and the stockholders,
I'm asking you to reassure them.

00:58:30.946 --> 00:58:32.072
I know you can do that.

00:58:32.156 --> 00:58:33.991
I can.

00:58:34.950 --> 00:58:36.535
But, Ms. Seo,

00:58:37.328 --> 00:58:39.621
I'm not exactly comfortable
with this situation either.

00:58:42.875 --> 00:58:46.670
My father wouldn't have been
comfortable either

00:58:46.754 --> 00:58:52.343
when you siphoned MANZAAR's designer
to launch a new brand.

00:58:52.426 --> 00:58:53.385
I know about that too.

00:58:54.470 --> 00:58:59.183
When my father was in the hospital,
he told me about that incident.

00:59:00.893 --> 00:59:05.439
He buried it without letting executives
or stockholders know, you know?

00:59:13.030 --> 00:59:15.532
He said,
"She'll help you out at least once."

00:59:17.493 --> 00:59:21.413
It's time for that one chance.

00:59:23.165 --> 00:59:24.249
Excuse me.

00:59:26.085 --> 00:59:27.211
One soju, please.

00:59:33.092 --> 00:59:34.093
At the time,

00:59:35.010 --> 00:59:37.721
he didn't even say he was disappointed.

00:59:37.805 --> 00:59:39.598
That's how he was.

00:59:40.933 --> 00:59:42.226
Chairman Seo Won-seok.

00:59:43.852 --> 00:59:45.104
Only this time.

00:59:45.646 --> 00:59:49.858
If there is any issue
with Director Seo Ji-woo again,

00:59:49.942 --> 00:59:53.028
your safety may not be guaranteed either.

00:59:53.946 --> 00:59:56.198
That's the atmosphere right now.

01:00:00.702 --> 01:00:01.703
Pour me a glass too.

01:00:11.171 --> 01:00:12.714
Thank you.

01:00:25.727 --> 01:00:27.980
I guess that's when.

01:00:28.063 --> 01:00:29.064
What's when?

01:00:30.607 --> 01:00:32.401
When you were hurt,

01:00:33.277 --> 01:00:35.612
Ji-woo must've found out then.

01:00:35.696 --> 01:00:37.156
Maybe that's why she left.

01:00:41.034 --> 01:00:43.287
Still, she grew up to be a bright person.

01:00:43.370 --> 01:00:44.621
Yes.

01:00:46.248 --> 01:00:47.541
Should we invite her for dinner?

01:00:48.667 --> 01:00:49.877
Kyeong-do will hate it.

01:00:51.837 --> 01:00:53.380
-Right?
-Yeah.

01:01:09.229 --> 01:01:11.732
You should've told me
that you were coming my house.

01:01:11.815 --> 01:01:13.525
I didn't know they invited you too.

01:01:14.610 --> 01:01:16.278
A son isn't a guest to invite.

01:01:16.361 --> 01:01:18.113
A guest would come when they're invited.

01:01:19.072 --> 01:01:20.782
You're normally at the laundromat.

01:01:20.866 --> 01:01:23.243
Here. Eat.

01:01:23.327 --> 01:01:27.247
Thank you. I absolutely love yukgaejang.

01:01:35.923 --> 01:01:36.757
Enjoy.

01:01:36.840 --> 01:01:38.717
Yes. Thank you for the food.

01:01:53.524 --> 01:01:54.900
Craving soju?

01:01:56.401 --> 01:01:59.196
People make that sound
when they have spicy food.

01:02:01.990 --> 01:02:06.828
You see, this is the exact taste
that I expected when I first saw it.

01:02:06.912 --> 01:02:10.040
You should have opened a restaurant
instead of a laundromat.

01:02:14.962 --> 01:02:16.088
Thank you for the food.

01:02:19.967 --> 01:02:22.052
Bulgogi too? Thank you.

01:02:25.889 --> 01:02:27.641
Can I have this bulgogi too?

01:02:28.225 --> 01:02:29.184
As much as you want.

01:02:33.772 --> 01:02:34.898
So full. Gosh.

01:02:36.483 --> 01:02:37.609
Here.

01:02:37.693 --> 01:02:39.027
That was a nice meal.

01:02:50.789 --> 01:02:51.623
ON MUTE

01:02:52.249 --> 01:02:54.084
-Baseball now?
-Well,

01:02:54.167 --> 01:02:55.419
I muted it.

01:02:56.128 --> 01:02:58.672
Stop watching baseball.
Now is so not the time.

01:03:00.299 --> 01:03:01.300
You see…

01:03:01.383 --> 01:03:02.426
What?

01:03:03.218 --> 01:03:06.263
Well… in my opinion…

01:03:07.097 --> 01:03:10.892
Quitting what you like, whatever it is…

01:03:14.271 --> 01:03:15.772
Well… it's crazy tough.

01:03:20.110 --> 01:03:23.322
Still, baseball isn't harmful.

01:03:23.405 --> 01:03:24.489
That's nice.

01:03:26.491 --> 01:03:29.161
It's healthy. It prevents dementia.

01:03:29.244 --> 01:03:30.078
Really?

01:03:30.912 --> 01:03:31.872
Better than Go-Stop?

01:03:31.955 --> 01:03:35.250
Why, Go-Stop has a risk of gambling.

01:03:36.460 --> 01:03:38.670
Yes. You're right.

01:03:39.796 --> 01:03:42.257
-It's a hit.
-What, really?

01:03:42.966 --> 01:03:45.594
What's the point of the other team's hit?

01:03:46.803 --> 01:03:48.639
Are you a Hanyeong fan?

01:03:49.890 --> 01:03:52.643
Have you seen them losing by 7-nil
then turning it around by 8 to 7?

01:03:53.352 --> 01:03:55.395
No. Unfortunately, I missed it.

01:03:55.479 --> 01:03:56.855
Do you like baseball?

01:03:56.938 --> 01:03:57.773
Kind of.

01:04:00.609 --> 01:04:03.111
-We have something in common.
-Of course.

01:04:03.195 --> 01:04:04.655
Let me give you a piece of apple.

01:04:05.822 --> 01:04:08.533
-I didn't peel it though.
-Thank you.

01:04:23.590 --> 01:04:26.635
Maybe if Seo Ji-yeon
was born out of wedlock...

01:04:26.718 --> 01:04:29.346
But Seo Ji-woo? And get rid of her?

01:04:31.264 --> 01:04:33.308
That won't affect the management.

01:04:33.850 --> 01:04:35.602
That's too weak. That won't do it.

01:04:35.686 --> 01:04:39.272
A KO isn't the only way to win.
You can also win by decision.

01:04:41.400 --> 01:04:44.152
Do you know
what Koreans are most sensitive about?

01:04:45.737 --> 01:04:46.738
Affairs.

01:04:48.115 --> 01:04:51.952
JARIM's dead Chairman Seo's wife
had an affair.

01:04:53.078 --> 01:04:55.414
And her daughter also has an affair.

01:05:01.086 --> 01:05:03.797
I think this alley is pretty. It's cozy.

01:05:07.008 --> 01:05:10.679
Maybe it's true that a married couple
has similar taste.

01:05:10.762 --> 01:05:11.722
You're copying me.

01:05:12.305 --> 01:05:13.974
Don't go overboard.

01:05:14.599 --> 01:05:15.475
Okay.

01:05:17.060 --> 01:05:18.854
I like how it sounds.

01:05:18.937 --> 01:05:20.063
Alley.

01:05:20.772 --> 01:05:22.107
Alleyway.

01:05:22.858 --> 01:05:24.234
Alley captain.

01:05:24.943 --> 01:05:26.069
Alley entrance.

01:05:29.656 --> 01:05:32.075
You should've stayed in the Culture Team.

01:05:38.331 --> 01:05:39.833
You know what?

01:05:40.542 --> 01:05:44.504
It feels weird
to have dinner together like this.

01:05:45.881 --> 01:05:47.466
Why?

01:05:48.091 --> 01:05:50.260
Is it like visiting your in-laws' house?

01:05:50.343 --> 01:05:51.595
No.

01:05:52.596 --> 01:05:53.847
I mean I like it.

01:05:55.015 --> 01:05:55.849
It's nice.

01:05:57.100 --> 01:06:00.061
It's like an alley. A cozy alley.

01:06:05.442 --> 01:06:08.612
Let's live like this alley.

01:06:11.823 --> 01:06:15.160
JARIM's dead Chairman Seo's wife
had an affair.

01:06:16.286 --> 01:06:18.705
And her daughter also has an affair.

01:06:19.581 --> 01:06:22.584
There will be a boycott of JARIM.

01:06:22.667 --> 01:06:26.213
It'll only be a matter of time
until the sisters get kicked out.

01:06:27.005 --> 01:06:30.258
And the company will be sold.

01:08:24.998 --> 01:08:28.209
So, you are… going?

01:08:29.544 --> 01:08:31.713
Don't you know what this field is like?

01:08:31.796 --> 01:08:34.174
It's better to hide. We might as well die!

01:08:35.425 --> 01:08:37.010
Just go live abroad.

01:08:37.093 --> 01:08:38.970
-Director Seo Ji-woo.
-Director Seo,

01:08:39.054 --> 01:08:41.681
don't you think that's irresponsible?

01:08:43.183 --> 01:08:46.061
Then let her live as an adulteress!

01:08:47.020 --> 01:08:49.147
I'm here
because the dog was barking too loud.

01:08:49.230 --> 01:08:51.107
Kang Min-woo,
you're out of bullets, right?

01:08:51.191 --> 01:08:54.361
I'll go, and if I can't bear it,
I'll come back.

01:08:55.862 --> 01:08:58.281
Ji-woo, let's…

01:08:59.616 --> 01:09:00.951
live well.